Q: Passing custom props to a react component using typescript A: <pre class="lang-jsx prettyprint-override"><code>interface Props {
  from: string;
  text: string;
}

const Message: React.FC&lt;Props&gt; = ({from, text}) =&gt; (
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;{text}&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;from: {from}&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;  
);
</code></pre>
<p>You just need to let Typescript know what the props for the component are.</p>
